{"duration_api_ms":593375,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"82312e0d-84f4-418f-aa4b-0abc53f02c04","total_cost_usd":22.817456500000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":200,"cache_creation_input_tokens":131535,"cache_read_input_tokens":38628858,"output_tokens":49349,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":12629},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":131535,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4105,"cache_read_input_tokens":456398,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1512},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":204,"outputTokens":49950,"thinkingTokens":12714,"cacheReadInputTokens":38677673,"cacheCreationInputTokens":222885,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":22.817456500000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":119,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Every batch-A finding (1–29) and all six decided items are in place. `dart analyze lib test` exits 0 (36 info-level notes, no errors or warnings) and `flutter test` passes 102/102. The Kotlin, Java, C++ and workflow changes are checked by reading only; they were not compiled.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe killed turn had finished findings 1–20; nothing in its edits was left half-done or inconsistent. It had investigated finding 21 but not edited it. Everything from finding 21 on was done this turn.\n\n**Done before the kill (checked against `git diff`):**\n\n1. **Document provider (Android):**\n   - `retrieveFile` rejects `.`, `..`, empty segments and NUL in the path, then checks that the resolved real path is still under its root.\n   - `isChildDocument` now matches whole path segments.\n   - Create and rename reject bad names.\n   - The `mt:*` calls require a write grant on the URI and, for subtree URIs, that the document is inside that subtree.\n   - The setting text warns that the files include the logged-in account's cookies and `access_key`.\n2. **Proxy:** turning on the proxy no longer turns off certificate checks for either HTTP client; only the \"禁用 SSL 证书验证\" switch does. The proxy dialog now explains this.\n3. **WebView:** mixed content is now `MIXED_CONTENT_NEVER_ALLOW`.\n4. **csrf on anonymous requests:** when a request goes out anonymously, `csrf`, `csrf_token` and `biliCSRF` are stripped along with `access_key`, including from form data.\n5. **SponsorBlock server:** requests are matched on the server's host instead of a raw prefix, so an empty address no longer affects every request. The dialog only saves a valid http(s) address with a host.\n6. **WebView reset:** \"重置cookie\" now counts as an account-cookie page, so the anonymous cookies are put back on close. `Accounts.clear` (used by 重置所有数据) wipes the WebView cookie store.\n7. **Linux WebView:** account cookies for notes and \"重置cookie\" are now session cookies, and the WebKit store is cleared when that window or page closes.\n8. **Cookie login:** keys and values are trimmed and values keep their `=` characters.\n9. **WBI keys:**\n   - A failed fetch is no longer cached; it falls back to the stored key.\n   - The date check compares year, month and day.\n   - `/nav` is fetched with the anonymous account.\n10. **Error toasts:** they show only scheme, host and path.\n11. **Redirects to another host:** the cookie, authorization and account headers and the old query parameters are dropped, and the account binding is set to `NoAccount`.\n12. **Note pages:** the account cookies and JS handlers apply only when the note page is opened from the video page, not from a link. `int.parse` became `tryParse`.\n13. **Note title:** it is URL-encoded in the note/add form body.\n14. **Settings import:** each section is validated before anything is cleared. A missing section leaves that box alone; if neither `setting` nor `video` is present the import throws.\n15. **Live danmaku:**\n   - The header check now requires 16 bytes and non-binary frames are ignored.\n   - The socket reports a drop, the controller clears its stream and reconnects with a fresh token, backing off from 2 to 30 seconds.\n   - Pausing or leaving the room cancels any pending reconnect.\n16. **Save original images (desktop):** copies instead of moving, and a failure no longer deletes cached files.\n17. **Download path change:** a new `reloadDownloadList()` pauses the running download and clears the list and waiting queue before re-reading; both settings entries use it.\n18. **Crash log:** it is now `librepili_logs.json` in the app's own data folder, emptied at start-up if it is over 2 MB. One failed write no longer breaks every later write.\n19. **Mobile 清除缓存:** skips `local_documents`.\n20. **Local follows import:** follows are re-keyed by their own `mid`.\n\n**Done this turn:**\n\n21. Danmaku is optional for a download: a failure no longer stops the video. With an unknown duration it fetches at least one segment.\n22. On each start the saved stream (video/audio id, codec and size, or durl segment sizes) is compared with the new one. If it differs, the partial files are deleted and the download restarts from zero. The old quality's folder is removed when the quality changes.\n23. WebDAV backup uploads to `<file>.tmp` and then renames it over the old file.\n24. + D6. WebDAV restore:\n   - Restore asks for confirmation first, naming what gets replaced.\n   - Every import (WebDAV or About) first saves a snapshot of settings and the local library to `<app data>/snapshots/before_import_<time>.json`, keeping the newest 5; the path is shown in a toast after a WebDAV restore.\n   - A \"恢复到导入前\" button on the WebDAV page restores the latest snapshot.\n25. CI stops with an error when a tagged release is requested without `SIGN_KEYSTORE_BASE64`.\n26. Windows no longer forwards a `--selftest` launch to a running instance. Linux makes existing relative file paths absolute before forwarding them.\n27. CI and manifest hygiene:\n   - Debug label is now \"LibrePili debug\".\n   - `READ_MEDIA_AUDIO` and `READ_MEDIA_VIDEO` are removed.\n   - `READ_MEDIA_IMAGES` and `WRITE_SETTINGS` are kept because they are used: `Permission.photos`, and `screen_brightness` system brightness in the player.\n   - Workflow jobs get `contents: write` instead of `write-all`.\n   - The 5 actions are pinned by commit SHA, resolved with `git ls-remote`.\n   - `appimagetool` is pinned to 1.9.1 with a sha256 check (`ed4ce84f…4eb0`, which I computed by downloading the file myself).\n28. \"查看完整更新\" links to `/commits/librepili`.\n29. Added the missing `return;` after the failed pre-captcha toast.\n\n**Decided items:**\n- **D1 (expired accounts):**\n   - `LoginAccount` has a persisted `expired` field (Hive field 4; older data reads as `false`).\n   - The two \"未登录\" paths call the new `Accounts.markExpired` instead of deleting the account.\n   - Expired accounts get no role in `Accounts.refresh` or `Accounts.set`.\n   - The account switcher and the logout dialog label them \"已失效\"; logging in again replaces the record.\n- **D4 (anti-fraud target check):**\n   - `AndroidHelper` checks the target app's SHA-256 signing-certificate fingerprint before sending cookies. If the check fails it sends nothing and shows a toast.\n   - A `<queries>` entry for the package was added.\n   - The repo has no authoritative fingerprint, so the list is empty and **the feature is off until one is added.** It needs the SHA-256 of the official `icu.freedomIntrovert.biliSendCommAntifraud` release's signing certificate, from `apksigner verify --print-certs <official apk>` (\"Signer #1 certificate SHA-256 digest\"), added to `ANTIFRAUD_CERT_SHA256`.\n- **D5:** only GET and HEAD are retried.\n- **D8 (comment anti-fraud check):**\n   - `LoginPolicy.explicitAccount` keeps an explicitly passed account in login mode only.\n   - The check's two \"as the account\" calls use `replyReplyList(asAccount: true)`; the anonymous half is unchanged.\n   - Three tests added to `login_policy_test.dart`, plus an expired-flag persistence test.\n- **D9 (credentials in settings export):**\n   - The credential keys are the WebDAV username and password and the SponsorBlock user ID; they are left out of exports unless the user confirms.\n   - Import keeps this device's values unless the file has them and the user confirms.\n   - This applies to both About import/export and WebDAV backup/restore.\n\n## Diff summary\n\n46 files, +983 −166. The largest changes:\n- `lib/utils/storage.dart`: +141 −12\n- `lib/services/download/download_service.dart`: +72\n- `AndroidHelper.java`: +61\n- `lib/pages/webview/view.dart`: +50\n- `BiliDocumentsProvider.kt`: +50\n- `lib/pages/live_room/controller.dart`: +47\n- `lib/pages/about/view.dart`: +45\n- `lib/pages/webdav/view.dart`: +45\n\n`audit-logs/route-pending.md` shows up in the diff but was already modified before this pass; I did not touch it.\n\n## Uncertainties\n\n- **Finding 1:** the real-path check also blocks symlinks inside the data folder that point outside it, such as `lib`. Those can't be opened or deleted through the provider any more. Whether MT Manager holds a write grant on the URIs it passes to `mt:*` calls is unverified; if it doesn't, those calls now fail.\n- **Finding 3:** the geetest captcha WebView still allows mixed content; it was not cited and changing it could break login.\n- **Finding 4:** stripping csrf also breaks the WBI signature of any anonymous request that carried csrf; such requests could not succeed anonymously anyway.\n- **Finding 11:** only the manual redirect path in the retry interceptor is covered.\n- **Finding 17:** a merge that is still running for the old folder can add its entry to the new folder's list when it finishes.\n- **Finding 18:** the old `.pili_logs.json` in Documents is left in place because it is shared with upstream.\n- **Finding 22:** a failed-merge restart now keeps its segments only if the stream is identical.\n- **Finding 26:** Windows detects `--selftest` by a substring match on the command line.\n- **Finding 27:**\n   - Removing `READ_MEDIA_AUDIO`/`READ_MEDIA_VIDEO` assumes no plugin needs them at runtime; I checked plugin manifests in the pub cache and found none.\n   - The CI-signing guard and the Actions pins can't be run here.\n- **D1:** an expired account can still be selected in the switcher, but it stays unused until the user logs in again. `refresh_token` is still unused, as route B doesn't need it.\n- **D6:** the snapshots contain credentials; they are stored in the app's private data folder. \"恢复到导入前\" exists only on the WebDAV page, although imports from About also create snapshots.\n- **D9:** WebDAV now asks up to two questions per backup and per restore.\n- I edited a few Dart files with small Python string replacements, not the Edit tool. Each result was checked with `git diff` and by the analyzer.\n\nThe scratchpad `probes/` folder has `cast_probe.dart`, `d3` and `head.diff`, which I did not create. The one file I did download there was deleted.\n\n```\nTEST RESULTS:\n  runner: flutter test (preceded by dart analyze lib test)\n  command: source local_env.sh && cd C:/Users/Z14/Documents/Coding/Piliplus && dart analyze lib test && flutter test\n  exit_code: 0\n  total: 102\n  passed: 102\n  failed: 0\n  skipped: 0\n  duration_ms: ~304000 (analyze ~280s, test ~24s)\n\nINFRA REPAIRS (during auto-repair, empty if none):\n\nREAL FAILURES (audit-fix-caused regressions, empty if none):\n\nINFRA-PERSISTENT (failures that hit the 3-cycle repair cap, empty if none):\n\nOVERALL: PASS\n```","ttft_ms":6937,"type":"result","duration_ms":968898,"uuid":"eaef0894-ac1f-466e-a839-ba492fc4379e","ttft_stream_ms":5921,"time_to_request_ms":588,"first_content_frame_ms":5922,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
